#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166784 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166622 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6f89636-f9bd-563d-a489-2a16746f8707" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/id #uuid "ff40db23-6bc1-539b-9f67-3c72c6f448d5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8405" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral\n$\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits} \\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^{1} \\sinh {\\left(2x+1\\right)} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu=2x+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x=\\dfrac 1 2 \\, \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & -2 & 1 \\\\ u & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{1}\\sinh (2x + 1)dx &= \\int_{-3}^{3}\\sinh u \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{-3}^{3}\\sinh udu \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{2}\\cosh u\\right|_{-3}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 3 - \\cosh (-3)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\cosh 3 - \\cosh 3) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6f89636-f9bd-563d-a489-2a16746f8707" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049599}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491349 :questio